WHAT THIS ESTABLISHES

ONE. The unit's coordinates are two kinds and nothing has said so. A MEASURED
coordinate carries a noise floor the corpus itself reports. A COMPUTED one
does not: bits per element is declared and exact, and so is error against a
rational reference. `101` noticed the first half of this and read it as a
caution about applying a tolerance band uniformly. It is more than that.

TWO. Over answer-equivalent arms the distinction is a nuisance. `100` prices
the whole cost of the flips at 0.045% to 3.83% of speed. Over answer-differing
arms the same flip is a change in the value the program computes, and part 2
shows it happening at six of the seven exchange rates swept. The seventh is
not a reprieve: at that rate the weighting is close enough to pure error that
the two lowest-error arms tie, and they tie because their errors are equal to
five figures rather than because the noise stopped mattering.

THREE. So there is a predicate on the mechanism the unit converged on, and it
is not a small one:

     A weighting may include a MEASURED coordinate only where every arm it
     ranges over computes the same answer. Where the arms disagree, every
     coordinate in the weighting must be computed or declared, because
     otherwise the program's output is a function of a benchmark's noise.

FOUR. And that lands on `100` section 6.1's Arm C, the band. A band accepts a
committed entry that is not the argmin. Over answer-equivalent arms that costs
a little speed, which is what `100` measures. Over answer-differing arms it
accepts a different ANSWER than the strategy names, which is not a cost to
trade. Arm C carries a predicate its statement does not: `holds where the arms
at the region compute the same value`.

FIVE. And the way out is not a restriction, it is a licence. Accuracy is
exactly computable, which p3 does and which the harness's own `score_output`
hook is shaped for. So the coordinate op's accuracy intent needs is a COMPUTED
one by nature, and it lands on the same side as bits per element rather than
on the timing side. The mechanism serves I7 and I5 once that is said out loud.
